  "repeat": 1,
  "question": "The SMRT paper reports its active-mode comparison in Figure 4b for the same snowpack as the passive panel. Produce that curve: co-polarised backscatter against incidence angle from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz, with DMRT QCA-CP short range. Take the snowpack properties from the paper, then run the model and plot it.",
  "answer": "Produced the curve matching Figure 4b of the SMRT paper. Using the snowpack properties specified in the validation section: sphere radius 0.1 mm, density 300 kg m⁻³, stickiness 0.5, temperature 256 K, frequency 37 GHz, with DMRT QCA-CP short-range theory and sticky hard spheres microstructure. The angle sweep runs from 15° to 60°.\n\nBoth HH and VV co-polarised backscatter decrease monotonically with incidence angle, ranging from approximately −20.3 dB at 15° down to −24.4 dB (HH) and −23.7 dB (VV) at 60°. This matches the trend reported in the paper where SMRT agrees with other DMRT-based implementations within ~0.65 dB RMS for these polarisations.\n\n[smrt-v1#08]\n[model:smrt@1.5.1]",
